schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: Knowledge Gardens
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: guide
  summary: >-
    How to build a community knowledge garden that survives contributor
    turnover: linking over filing, openly-marked growth stages
    (seedling/budding/evergreen), and active tending by a named gardener.
    Uses SuperBenefit's public Knowledge Garden as a worked model (Docs,
    Lexicon, Links, Patterns) and recommends plain markdown + Git (Obsidian
    + Quartz + GitHub) as the durable, non-lock-in tool stack.
  audience: community organizers and local-node stewards building a team knowledge commons
  known_tensions:
    - >-
      polished, collaboration-friendly tools (Notion) vs. durable,
      portable-in-plain-text tools (Markdown + Git) — the article resolves
      this as "own your source of truth in plain text and Git; use anything
      prettier as a window onto it, not the vault itself"
  related_concepts:
    - Digital Garden (seedling/budding/evergreen)
    - knowledge commons
  related_resources:
    - Obsidian
    - Quartz
    - SuperBenefit Knowledge Garden
    - GravityDAO
  maturity: raw
  public_use: source-linked-unreviewed
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/knowledge-gardens.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted

# assessed-but-excluded:
